    "id": "chord-symbols",
    "title": "Chord symbol catalog",
    "description": "Every built-in chord suffix, with its aliases and the intervals it sounds.",
    "text": "# Chord symbol catalog\n\nEvery built-in chord suffix, with its aliases and the intervals it sounds.\n\nA [chord symbol](https://pkhambat.mintlify.site/pitched/chords#chord-symbols) is a root, a suffix and an optional bass. This page lists every suffix the language knows by name. Suffixes outside this list can be [composed with modifiers](https://pkhambat.mintlify.site/pitched/chords#composing-a-suffix).\n\n## Reading the catalog\n\nEach row is one chord quality. Its suffixes are aliases: they sound identical. Suffixes are case-sensitive. The intervals are counted from the root against the major scale: `3` is a major third, `b3` a minor third, `#5` an augmented fifth, `bb7` a diminished seventh. `9`, `11` and `13` sound an octave above `2`, `4` and `6`. The list is exactly what sounds, so a quality that omits its fifth shows no `5`.\n\nAfter a degree, a suffix cannot start with a digit; see [Chords by degree](https://pkhambat.mintlify.site/pitched/chords#chords-by-degree). The preferred spellings below work after both letters and degrees unless noted.\n\n## Preferred spellings\n\n| Quality | After a letter | After a degree |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Major | (none) | `M` |\n| Minor | `m` | `m` |\n| Diminished | `dim` | `dim` |\n| Augmented | `aug` | `aug` |\n| Suspended second, fourth | `sus2`, `sus4` | `sus2`, `sus4` |\n| Major seventh | `maj7` | `maj7` |\n| Dominant seventh | `7` | `dom7` |\n| Minor seventh | `m7` | `m7` |\n| Half-diminished | `m7b5` | `m7b5` |\n| Diminished seventh | `dim7` | `dim7` |\n| Major 6/9, minor 6/9 | `6/9`, `m6/9` | `M6/9`, `m6/9` |\n\n## Major and dominant\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `13` | `1 3 5 b7 9 13` |\n| `13#11`, `13+4`, `13#4` | `1 3 5 b7 9 #11 13` |\n| `13#9` | `1 3 5 b7 #9 13` |\n| `13#9#11` | `1 3 5 b7 #9 #11 13` |\n| `13b9` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 13` |\n| `13b9#11` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 #11 13` |\n| `13no5` | `1 3 b7 9 13` |\n| `6`, `add6`, `add13`, `M6` | `1 3 5 6` |\n| `6/9` | `1 3 5 6 9` |\n| `7`, `dom` | `1 3 5 b7` |\n| `7#11`, `7#4` | `1 3 5 b7 #11` |\n| `7#11b13`, `7b5b13` | `1 3 5 b7 #11 b13` |\n| `7#9` | `1 3 5 b7 #9` |\n| `7#9#11`, `7b5#9`, `7#9b5` | `1 3 5 b7 #9 #11` |\n| `7#9#11b13` | `1 3 5 b7 #9 #11 b13` |\n| `7#9b13` | `1 3 5 b7 #9 b13` |\n| `7add6`, `67`, `7add13` | `1 3 5 b7 13` |\n| `7b13` | `1 3 b7 b13` |\n| `7b6` | `1 3 5 b6 b7` |\n| `7b9` | `1 3 5 b7 b9` |\n| `7b9#11`, `7b5b9`, `7b9b5` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 #11` |\n| `7b9#9` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 #9` |\n| `7b9b13` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 b13` |\n| `7b9b13#11`, `7b9#11b13`, `7b5b9b13` | `1 3 5 b7 b9 #11 b13` |\n| `7no5` | `1 3 b7` |\n| `9` | `1 3 5 b7 9` |\n| `9#11`, `9+4`, `9#4` | `1 3 5 b7 9 #11` |\n| `9#11b13`, `9b5b13` | `1 3 5 b7 9 #11 b13` |\n| `9b13` | `1 3 b7 9 b13` |\n| `9no5` | `1 3 b7 9` |\n| `alt7` | `1 3 b7 b9` |\n| `M`, `^`, Empty suffix, `maj` | `1 3 5` |\n| `M13#11`, `maj13#11`, `M13+4`, `M13#4` | `1 3 5 7 9 #11 13` |\n| `M6#11`, `M6b5`, `6#11`, `6b5` | `1 3 5 6 #11` |\n| `M7add13` | `1 3 5 6 7 9` |\n| `M7b6`, `^7b6` | `1 3 b6 7` |\n| `M7b9` | `1 3 5 7 b9` |\n| `Madd9`, `2`, `add9`, `add2` | `1 3 5 9` |\n| `Maddb9` | `1 3 5 b9` |\n| `maj#4`, `Δ#4`, `Δ#11`, `M7#11`, `^7#11`, `maj7#11` | `1 3 5 7 #11` |\n| `maj13`, `Maj13`, `^13` | `1 3 5 7 9 13` |\n| `maj7`, `Δ`, `ma7`, `M7`, `Maj7`, `^7` | `1 3 5 7` |\n| `maj7#9#11` | `1 3 5 7 #9 #11` |\n| `maj9`, `Δ9`, `^9` | `1 3 5 7 9` |\n| `maj9#11`, `Δ9#11`, `^9#11` | `1 3 5 7 9 #11` |\n\n## Minor\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `m`, `min`, `-` | `1 b3 5` |\n| `m11`, `-11` | `1 b3 5 b7 9 11` |\n| `m13`, `-13` | `1 b3 5 b7 9 13` |\n| `m6`, `-6` | `1 b3 5 6` |\n| `m6/9` | `1 b3 5 6 9` |\n| `m7`, `min7`, `mi7`, `-7` | `1 b3 5 b7` |\n| `m7#5` | `1 b3 b6 b7` |\n| `m7add11`, `m7add4` | `1 b3 5 b7 11` |\n| `m9`, `-9` | `1 b3 5 b7 9` |\n| `m9#5` | `1 b3 b6 b7 9` |\n| `madd4` | `1 b3 4 5` |\n| `madd9` | `1 b3 5 9` |\n| `mb6b9` | `1 b3 b6 b9` |\n| `mb6M7` | `1 b3 b6 7` |\n| `mM7`, `mMaj7`, `-Δ7`, `mΔ`, `-^7`, `-maj7` | `1 b3 5 7` |\n| `mM9`, `mMaj9`, `-^9` | `1 b3 5 7 9` |\n| `mMaj7b6` | `1 b3 5 b6 7` |\n| `mMaj9b6` | `1 b3 5 b6 7 9` |\n\n## Diminished and flat fifth\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `13b5` | `1 3 b5 6 b7 9` |\n| `7b5` | `1 3 b5 b7` |\n| `9b5` | `1 3 b5 b7 9` |\n| `dim`, `°`, `o` | `1 b3 b5` |\n| `dim7`, `°7`, `o7` | `1 b3 b5 bb7` |\n| `m7b5`, `ø`, `-7b5`, `h7`, `h` | `1 b3 b5 b7` |\n| `M7b5` | `1 3 b5 7` |\n| `m9b5` | `1 2 b3 b5 b7` |\n| `M9b5` | `1 3 b5 7 9` |\n| `Mb5` | `1 3 b5` |\n| `o7M7` | `1 b3 b5 6 7` |\n| `oM7` | `1 b3 b5 7` |\n\n## Augmented and sharp fifth\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `+add#9` | `1 3 #5 #9` |\n| `7#5`, `+7`, `7+`, `7aug`, `aug7` | `1 3 #5 b7` |\n| `7#5#9`, `7#9#5`, `7alt` | `1 3 #5 b7 #9` |\n| `7#5b9`, `7b9#5` | `1 3 #5 b7 b9` |\n| `7#5b9#11` | `1 3 #5 b7 b9 #11` |\n| `7#5sus4` | `1 4 #5 b7` |\n| `9#5`, `9+` | `1 3 #5 b7 9` |\n| `9#5#11` | `1 3 #5 b7 9 #11` |\n| `aug`, `+`, `+5`, `^#5` | `1 3 #5` |\n| `m#5`, `-#5`, `m+` | `1 b3 #5` |\n| `M#5add9`, `+add9` | `1 3 #5 9` |\n| `m11A` | `1 b3 #5 b7 9 11` |\n| `M7#5sus4` | `1 4 #5 7` |\n| `M9#5sus4` | `1 4 #5 7 9` |\n| `maj7#5`, `maj7+5`, `+maj7`, `^7#5` | `1 3 #5 7` |\n| `maj9#5`, `Maj9#5` | `1 3 #5 7 9` |\n\n## Suspended and fourth-based\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `13sus4`, `13sus` | `1 4 5 b7 9 13` |\n| `4`, `quartal` | `1 4 b7 b10` |\n| `7sus4`, `7sus` | `1 4 5 b7` |\n| `7sus4b9b13`, `7b9b13sus4` | `1 4 5 b7 b9 b13` |\n| `9sus4`, `9sus` | `1 4 5 b7 9` |\n| `M7sus4` | `1 4 5 7` |\n| `M9sus4` | `1 4 5 7 9` |\n| `phryg`, `7b9sus`, `7b9sus4` | `1 4 5 b7 b9` |\n| `sus24`, `sus4add9` | `1 2 4 5` |\n| `sus4`, `sus` | `1 4 5` |\n\n## Other voicings\n\n| Suffixes after an absolute root | Chord intervals |\n| --- | --- |\n| `11` | `1 5 b7 9 11` |\n| `11b9` | `1 5 b7 b9 11` |\n| `5` | `1 5` |\n| `sus2` | `1 2 5` |\n\n## Spelling restrictions\n\n- A 6/9 chord is `6/9` or `m6/9`. `69`, `m69`, `6add9` and `maj6/9` are errors.\n- After a degree, `6/9` alone would read as a bass: `6/9` is the chord on degree 6 over degree 9. Write `1M6/9`.\n- `b9sus` cannot follow a letter root directly: `Cb9sus` is C flat with the suffix `9sus`. For C with a flat ninth and a suspended fourth, write `C7b9sus4`.\n- `°` and `ø` are accepted after a letter root only.\n- An interval function can produce tones that match no row here. `print` then shows the tones without a chord name.\n"
